# Fixture data must round-trip byte-identically on every platform. Git's
# text auto-detection plus core.autocrlf=true (GitHub Windows runners default)
# inflates text-detected fixtures with CRLF on checkout, so byte comparisons
# against their binary-detected .zst counterparts fail (decodecorpus WrongSize
# on Windows CI). Rules are grouped per fixture family; extend the group when
# a family gains a directory instead of adding one-off entries.

# Decode/encode corpus: originals and compressed frames.
crates/zstdx/decodecorpus_files/** binary
crates/zstdx/test_fixtures/** binary

# Dictionary fixtures: the trained dictionary and its training corpus.
crates/zstdx/dict_tests/** binary

# Fuzz regression artifacts: arbitrary-byte crash inputs, some text-detected.
crates/zstdx-fuzz/artifacts/** binary

# Compressed frames also land outside the fixture directories.
*.zst binary
